1
00:00:01,609 --> 00:00:04,764
(Q1) Jim: Hello, South City Cycling Club.&nbsp;

2
00:00:04,764 --> 00:00:06,593
Woman: Oh, hi.

3
00:00:06,593 --> 00:00:11,037
Er ... I want to find out about joining the club.

4
00:00:11,037 --> 00:00:11,956
Jim: Right.&nbsp;

5
00:00:11,956 --> 00:00:13,157
I can help you there.

6
00:00:13,157 --> 00:00:17,422
[Example] I'm the club secretary and my name's Jim Hunter.

7
00:00:17,422 --> 00:00:19,421
Woman: Oh, hi Jim.

8
00:00:19,421 --> 00:00:23,651
Jim: So, are you interested in membership for yourself?&nbsp;

9
00:00:23,651 --> 00:00:25,674
Woman: That's right.

10
00:00:25,674 --> 00:00:27,091
Jim: OK. Jim：

11
00:00:27,091 --> 00:00:30,900
Well there are basically two types of adult membership.

12
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:36,186
If you're pretty serious about cycling, there's the Full membership.

13
00:00:36,186 --> 00:00:50,163
[Q1答案句： races， not only ... but also = and] That costs 260 dollars and that covers you not just for ordinary cycling but also for races both here in the city and also in other parts of Australia.

14
00:00:50,163 --> 00:00:51,472
(Q2) Woman: Right.

15
00:00:51,472 --> 00:00:54,200
Well, I'm not really up to that standard.

16
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:59,439
I was more interested in just joining a group to do some cycling in my free time.

17
00:00:59,439 --> 00:01:00,898
Jim: Sure.&nbsp;

18
00:01:00,898 --> 00:01:03,105
That's why most people join.

19
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:08,197
[Q2跟定位词] So, in that case you'd be better with the Recreational membership.

20
00:01:08,197 --> 00:01:15,956
That's 108 dollars if you're over 19, and 95 dollars if you're under.&nbsp;

21
00:01:15,956 --> 00:01:17,707
Woman: I'm 25.

22
00:01:17,707 --> 00:01:19,751
Jim: OK. Jim：

23
00:01:19,751 --> 00:01:26,008
It's paid quarterly, and you can upgrade it later to the Full membership if you want to, of course.

24
00:01:26,008 --> 00:01:39,650
[Q2答案句： insurance。 空前and , also=and] Now both types of membership include the club fee of 20 dollars.&nbsp; &nbsp;They also provide insurance in case you have an accident, though we hope you won't need that, of course.

25
00:01:39,650 --> 00:01:41,067
Woman: No.

26
00:01:41,067 --> 00:01:45,327
(Q3) OK, well, I'll go with the Recreational membership, I think.

27
00:01:45,327 --> 00:01:49,290
And that allows me to join in the club activities, and so on?

28
00:01:49,290 --> 00:01:50,558
Jim: That's right. Jim：

29
00:01:50,558 --> 00:01:56,897
And once you're a member of the club, you're also permitted to wear our kit when you're out cycling.

30
00:01:56,897 --> 00:01:58,780
It's green and white.

31
00:01:58,780 --> 00:02:02,545
Woman: Yes, I've seen cyclists wearing it.

32
00:02:02,545 --> 00:02:04,567
So, can I buy that at the club?

33
00:02:04,567 --> 00:02:19,131
[Q3答案句： 拼写] Jim: No, it's made to order by a company in Brisbane.&nbsp; &nbsp;You can find them online: they're called Jerriz. That's J-E-R-R-l-Z.

34
00:02:19,131 --> 00:02:23,612
You can use your membership number to put in an order on their website.

35
00:02:23,612 --> 00:02:24,964
Woman: OK.

36
00:02:24,964 --> 00:02:28,810
(Q4) Now, can you tell me a bit about the rides I can do?

37
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:29,915
Jim: Sure.&nbsp;

38
00:02:29,915 --> 00:02:43,451
[Q4跟定位： cycling skills] So we have training rides pretty well every morning, and they're a really good way of improving your cycling skills as well as your general level of fitness, but they're different levels.

39
00:02:43,451 --> 00:02:50,835
Level A is pretty fast - you're looking at about 30 or 35 kilometres an hour.&nbsp;

40
00:02:50,835 --> 00:03:04,079
[Q4答案句：25] If you can do about 25 kilometres an hour, you'd probably be level B, and then level C are the novices, who stay at about 15 kilometres per hour.

41
00:03:04,079 --> 00:03:05,262
Woman: Right.

42
00:03:05,262 --> 00:03:07,982
Well I reckon I'd be level B.

43
00:03:07,982 --> 00:03:11,057
(Q5) So, when are the sessions for that level?

44
00:03:11,057 --> 00:03:13,810
Jim: There are a couple each week. Jim：

45
00:03:13,810 --> 00:03:16,416
They're both early morning sessions.

46
00:03:16,416 --> 00:03:26,880
[Q5答案句： stadium] There's one on Tuesdays, and for that one you meet at 5.30 am, and the meeting point's the stadium - do you know where that is?

47
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:29,785
Woman: Yes, it's quite near my home, in fact.

48
00:03:29,785 --> 00:03:33,009
(Q6) OK, and how about the other one?

49
00:03:33,009 --> 00:03:40,362
[Q6答案句： park.      main gate = entrance] Jim: That's on Thursdays.&nbsp; It starts at the same time, but they meet at the main gate to the park.

50
00:03:40,362 --> 00:03:43,492
Woman: Is that the one just past the shopping mall?

51
00:03:43,492 --> 00:03:45,702
Jim: That's it. Jim：

52
00:03:45,702 --> 00:03:47,963
(Q7) [也可能没有小标题， 直接就过渡] Woman: So how long are the rides?

53
00:03:47,963 --> 00:03:51,131
[跟定位] Jim: They're about an hour and a half.&nbsp;

54
00:03:51,131 --> 00:03:55,570
So, if you have a job it's easy to fit in before you go to work.

55
00:03:55,570 --> 00:04:02,417
[Q7答案句：coffee， go +地点 for ...= have ...] And the members often go somewhere for coffee afterwards, so it's quite a social event.

56
00:04:02,417 --> 00:04:05,055
Woman: OK. That sounds good.

57
00:04:05,055 --> 00:04:09,783
(Q8) I've only just moved to the city so I don't actually know many people yet.

58
00:04:09,783 --> 00:04:13,393
Jim: Well, it's a great way to meet people. Jim：

59
00:04:13,393 --> 00:04:25,300
[Q8答案句： leader。 算前置，但猜不到 ，  所以跟疑似词] Woman: And does each ride have a leader?&nbsp;Jim: Sometimes, but not always.&nbsp; &nbsp;But you don't really need one; the group members on the ride support one another, anyway.

60
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:27,694
(Q9) Woman: How would we know where to go?

61
00:04:27,694 --> 00:04:38,214
[Q9答案句： route。 代词指代 print that out] Jim: If you check the club website, you'll see that the route for each ride is clearly marked.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; So you can just print that out and take it along with you.

62
00:04:38,214 --> 00:04:44,680
It's similar from one week to another, but it's not always exactly the same.

63
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:47,713
(Q10) Woman: And what do I need to bring?

64
00:04:47,713 --> 00:04:51,303
Jim: Well, bring a bottle of water, and your phone.&nbsp;

65
00:04:51,303 --> 00:04:55,393
You shouldn't use it while you're cycling, but have it with you.

66
00:04:55,393 --> 00:04:56,690
Woman: Right.

67
00:04:56,690 --> 00:05:05,217
[Q10答案句，同替] Jim: And in winter, it's well before sunrise when we set out, so you need to make sure your bike's got lights.&nbsp;

68
00:05:05,217 --> 00:05:10,458
Woman: That's OK. Well, thanks Jim. I'd definitely like to join.

69
00:05:10,458 --> 00:05:13,150
So what's the best way of going about it?

70
00:05:13,150 --> 00:05:15,650
Jim: You can... Jim：

